A||||2||Sandman||Turbo for a 4 cyl ???
Z||000000||Sandman||04-03-99||03:38 PM||||I have a turbo off of a 84 Pont. Sunbird.  Does anyone know if it will work on a 84 Fiero 4 cyl.?  Will the engine hold up with the increased horse power?
Z||000001||theogre||04-04-99||12:15 AM||||need a bit more data dude.<p>what motor was in the sunbird? if it was another 4 cyl and with in about 1/2 litre displacement in size, technically yes it could be used. Practicality is another matter.<p>Odd are, the turbo needs rebuilding, and if posible an adjustable waste gate link installed. You'll need to have all the requisite exhaust and intake parts custom made.<p>Fiero stock 4 cyls will not take a large boost. they are just not very strong mechanically. 5-7PSI is probably max, and maybe not even that if the motor isn't in top shape. (The SD4 that you often hear about on the other hand easily would take 10PSI)
Z||000002||Motorhead||04-04-99||04:53 AM||||I've never even considered putting a turbo on my 4-cylinder Fiero, this engine is famous for throwing rods and cracking heads, IMO it wouldn't last very long. <p>I have a Datsun 280ZX turbo and have found that turbo components are quite expensive. If your after better performance, it would probably be more cost effective to go with a V6 and be done with it.<p>Just my 2-cents!<br>
